<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Adansi</h1><p class="st-meta">1550 CE – 1650 CE (approx.) · capital Fomena</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Early Akan kingdom of the central forest, remembered as one of the first Akan states before its conquest by Denkyira.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Adansi lay in the forest south of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>, with its capital at Fomena. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> tradition regards it as one of the earliest organised Akan states, and its name is linked in tradition with building, as its people were said to be the first to construct houses in the forest.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its rulers controlled gold mining and the trade routes from the central forest toward the coast and northern markets. Several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> clans trace their early migrations through Adansi, and its political forms, including the stool and matrilineal succession, were shared by later states.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 17th century Adansi was conquered by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/denkyira">Denkyira</a> and then passed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>. Fomena later gave its name to the 1874 treaty that ended the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> war, and Adansi remains a traditional area in Ghana.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1550 CE – 1650 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:90.55%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1550 CE – 1650 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Fomena</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Akan religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Twi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ghana">Ghana</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Adansi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-adansi" aria-label="Kingdom of Adansi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4638 1943 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Adansi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4958 2199L4949 2199M4958 2199L4973 2230"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4949 2199h0M4973 2230h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4958 2199h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4958 2199h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Fomena. <a href="/atlas?year=1600&amp;focus=kingdom-of-adansi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

